1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:07,360
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

2
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:13,400
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

3
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:14,660
Woah

4
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,760
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

5
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:25,460
nezumiiro no sora no shita

6
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:31,700
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:37,800
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

8
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,980
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

9
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:50,000
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

10
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:56,960
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

11
00:00:57,060 --> 00:01:02,540
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

12
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:09,140
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

13
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:14,900
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

14
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:21,100
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

15
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:28,100
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

16
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,020
A smoke bomb and a grenade in one.

17
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,300
That reckless fool is
beginning to annoy me.

18
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,120
Do you think you can follow their scent?

19
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,240
Uh-huh!

20
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:04,480
Here, officer.

21
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:08,620
Take her somewhere she'll be safe.

22
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,300
Winry, Al is still
fighting, so I have to go.

23
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:14,640
Okay?

24
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:16,500
Okay? I'm sorry.

25
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:19,220
When this is over, I'll explain everything.

26
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:35,960
Why?
Why is waiting the only thing I can do?

27
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,240
We have a girl in custody
in Sector 8 who appears

28
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,100
to be a friend of the
Fullmetal Alchemist.

29
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:46,120
Escort her to Central Command.
Repeat, Sector 8.

30
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:48,920
We have a girl in custody who appears
to be a friend of the Fullmetal Alchemist...

31
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,300
It's just about time.

32
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:51,780
...Escort her to Central Command.

33
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,300
Go and back them up.

34
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:54,220
Right.

35
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,300
There's a vacant house outside of town.

36
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:02,300
That's where we'll meet up.

37
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:03,580
Don't be followed.

38
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:04,540
Okay.

39
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:08,300
If something goes wrong, I'll let you know.

40
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,300
All right.

41
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,660
And Sir, please stay out of the field.

42
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:17,400
I know, Lieutenant. Now go.

43
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,300
You won't give up.

44
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,140
This area looks deserted.

45
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,000
A dead end. We're trapped.

46
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:40,700
Hmm?

47
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,620
Scar again.

48
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:45,740
Gluttony, go see what he's up to this time.

49
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:48,780
And I'll take care of our
two little friends here.

50
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,300
What happened to me?

51
00:03:57,460 --> 00:03:58,300
What's wrong?

52
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:00,300
My arm. My lord.

53
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:03,300
I'm useless to you now.

54
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,300
What are you talking about?

55
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:08,040
You cannot burden yourself with me.

56
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,300
If you do, they'll only get you too.

57
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:13,020
A king is no king without his people,

58
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:16,040
But a people without their
king would be lost as well.

59
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:17,880
You can't do that to them.

60
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:20,020
My lord, think of our clan!

61
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,040
You must live for their sake.

62
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,580
I won't leave you!

63
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:27,780
Sometimes someone must be left behind.

64
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,300
For the greater good.

65
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:33,660
Lan Fan? What are you planning?!

66
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:35,300
No! Don't do it!

67
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,520
Watch out!

68
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:53,080
There's nothing inside that armor.
You're hollow, aren't you?

69
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,100
You poor boy.

70
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:59,300
Alchemy trapped you in that metal prison
and yet you still have faith in it.

71
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:09,800
True, there are plenty of things
about this body that are inconvenient.

72
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:11,820
But it's nothing I can't live with.

73
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:13,500
I don't need pity from anyone.

74
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:15,080
Least of all from you.

75
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:18,720
My brother used alchemy to save my life.

76
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:23,060
To regret the form I have now would
mean not only rejecting alchemy,

77
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:25,300
but also turning my back on him.

78
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:28,040
I believe in my brother
and I believe in alchemy.

79
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,480
I will not lose faith.

80
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,900
I want to believe!

81
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:32,100
Oh, do you?

82
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:45,300
Brother, where's Winry?

83
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,460
She's safe.

84
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:48,960
No thanks to me, though.

85
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:50,880
I made her cry again.

86
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,860
You really should be more careful, brother.

87
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,960
She doesn't like to
see you fight like that.

88
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,140
Yeah.

89
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:02,800
But she's gone now.

90
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:04,060
Let's end this!

91
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,960
Oh, I found you!

92
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,400
The Ishvalan!

93
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,760
You again.

94
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,300
Look at his tattoo!

95
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,500
Homunculus.

96
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,400
Huh?

97
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,480
It's Ling!

98
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,800
Go! Move it!

99
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:01,760
[GASP]

100
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,300
Get me some strong cable.

101
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:16,620
Right! On it!

102
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:22,860
Your own regenerative ability
is working against you.

103
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:25,720
Your flesh won't stop expanding .

104
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:28,300
It'll keep you tied up nice and tight.

105
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:30,300
You're mine now,

106
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:32,300
Homunculus!

107
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:44,800
That was well played, girl.

108
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:52,880
I beat you.

109
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:58,360
How does it feel to be tricked?

110
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,020
You lose this round.

111
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,840
What?

112
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:04,060
That thing is a Homunculus?

113
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,840
Put him in. We're getting out of here.

114
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:15,620
Huh?

115
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,160
Ah!

116
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,580
Hold on a sec, Lieutenant.

117
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:30,660
Shh!

118
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:35,600
- Wait! What's going on?
- Al!

119
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,920
The MPs are watching.

120
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:40,360
Just pretend we don't know her.

121
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,140
They're getting away! After them!

122
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:43,840
Right!

123
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:47,300
The Colonel may be a creep and a jerk,
but at least we can trust him.

124
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:49,280
We have something to do.

125
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:02,300
We have to get him, Al!

126
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:06,220
You killed the Rockbells
and Nina, among many others!

127
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:08,500
You're going to answer for your crimes!

128
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,640
Are these two giving you trouble, servant?

129
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:23,480
This is the servant of the
man who saved my life.

130
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:26,060
You better leave him alone,
puny little boy!

131
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:28,280
Wait a sec! Who are you calling puny?!

132
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,880
Where'd that kid come from?

133
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,760
Get away, girl. It's dangerous.

134
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:35,700
They've got us outnumbered.

135
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:38,180
It's time for us to retreat!

136
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,120
Ha!

137
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:50,000
Ah!

138
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:55,020
[COUGHING]

139
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:58,660
What kind of alchemy was that?

140
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,900
She did it from that far away?

141
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:02,280
Here, follow me.

142
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:06,980
I can't see.

143
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:09,040
Scar!

144
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:12,820
[CAR HORN, TIRES SCREECHING]

145
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:16,280
I know who you are, Ling Yao.
Don't worry.

146
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:18,800
We're on our way to a secure safe house.

147
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,860
My friend! I left her behind.

148
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:21,760
Go get her!

149
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:22,560
What?!

150
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,520
No, we can't. We don't have time.

151
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,340
Make time! She could be dying now.

152
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:29,400
She's still waiting there for me!

153
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,900
You had better make it quick.

154
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:38,680
[CAR HORN]

155
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,100
Huh?

156
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:47,120
That woman driving...

157
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,060
I'm sure she's Mustang's.

158
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:56,300
I'm tired of playing
games with that upstart.

159
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:02,300
Fullmetal Alchemist.

160
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:11,240
Her eyes... Is that
how mine looked?

161
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:18,680
No matter what I do,
hatred only breeds more hatred.

162
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,300
There you go.
I think I managed to stop the bleeding.

163
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:26,700
Thank you.

164
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,840
Sir, the MPs are all closing in on us.

165
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:34,380
We need to get going.

166
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:35,900
He took a shot to the leg.

167
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:38,080
In his condition,
he couldn't have gotten far.

168
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,820
- Comb the area for him!
-[DOGS BARKING]

169
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:40,580
Sir!

170
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,500
Quickly, sir! Quickly!

171
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:45,680
Xiao-Mei, where are you?

172
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:47,900
Oh, no.

173
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,080
Look what I found, Ed!

174
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:57,580
We're a little busy right now
to be adopting panda bears, Al!

175
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:00,720
I couldn't leave her alone in the
middle of all that mess back there!

176
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,560
First stray cats and now this!

177
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:05,600
Just how many animals can you
stuff into that armor of yours, huh?!

178
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,500
Get rid of it!

179
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:08,360
What a heartless thing to say!

180
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,800
Look how sweet and gentle she is.

181
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,360
[TINY GROWL]

182
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:16,940
[GIGGLES]
It's all right, you're safe now.

183
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:31,160
This way. Follow me.

184
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,120
Thanks.

185
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:35,860
You can stay in here, okay?

186
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:45,300
Hey, Winry!

187
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:48,620
Oh!

188
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:51,300
Hello there, Fullmetal Alchemist.

189
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:53,660
Fuhrer Bradley, this is a surprise.

190
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:55,300
What brings you here?

191
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,680
I heard that a childhood
friend of yours was

192
00:12:57,690 --> 00:13:00,300
under our protection here
at the Command Center.

193
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:05,700
As a friend of such an important alchemist,
she deserves our every courtesy.

194
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,280
I should be on my way now.

195
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,300
If you'll please excuse me, miss.

196
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,580
Oh, of course, sir.

197
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,960
That's a nice, honest
friend you've got there.

198
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:22,260
Make sure you both take good care of her.

199
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,440
Ed?

200
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:32,640
Huh?

201
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,740
You promised.

202
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:37,160
Tell me everything about my parents.

203
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:39,120
What happened to them?

204
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,480
I see.

205
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:56,300
They did everything they could to
help others, right up until the end.

206
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:59,060
But I...

207
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:01,740
I just wish they could have
come back to me alive.

208
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:03,560
Is that selfish?

209
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:06,900
More waiting.

210
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:09,980
That's all I can ever do.

211
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,420
Ah, perfect timing.

212
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:29,040
Miss Rockbell, there's
a telephone call for you.

213
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,080
For me?

214
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:35,160
Yes, hello?

215
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,580
Oh, Mr. Garfiel!

216
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:39,300
I'm sorry about this, Winry...

217
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:43,360
I know you've got a lot going on,
and I tried to handle it myself, really.

218
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,540
- Where is she?
- Isn't Winry back yet?

219
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:47,920
Look at this!
Winry's the only one who can fix it.

220
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:51,300
But I can't take this anymore,
your customers are so needy!

221
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:54,420
Please hurry back, Winry! We miss you!

222
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:56,540
You there, Miss Winry?

223
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:57,480
Tetsu?

224
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,640
Please come back to the shop soon.

225
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:03,220
You do a much better job working
on my leg than Mr. Garfiel can!

226
00:15:03,220 --> 00:15:04,480
We need you here!

227
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:06,580
Yeah, another thing, Winry,

228
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:10,100
We still need an outer covering
for that model leg you made for me.

229
00:15:10,100 --> 00:15:12,860
- My arm needs work, too!
- Hey, hold on a sec! I was first!

230
00:15:12,860 --> 00:15:13,980
Miss you, Winry!

231
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:16,940
You idiot, of course you miss her!
We all do.

232
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:18,300
Isn't that the truth!

233
00:15:18,900 --> 00:15:20,200
I'm sorry.

234
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,340
I'll be back home soon.

235
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,240
Just hold on.

236
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:26,740
I won't be much longer.

237
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:28,460
I'll help everyone.

238
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,360
Thank you all.

239
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:43,120
Thank you both...
for stopping me back there.

240
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:47,560
I forgot there were still
people who depended on me.

241
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:51,800
If I had done it, I wouldn't have
been able to face them again.

242
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,640
Of course.

243
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:59,400
I expect you to take good
care of your auto mail.

244
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,380
Yep.

245
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:03,480
Oh, and I'll send you some
good polishing oil soon, Al.

246
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:04,600
Great!

247
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:08,900
And no dying, okay?

248
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:10,380
Right.

249
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:13,040
Oh, and...

250
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:17,340
The next time I make you cry,
I hope that they'll be...[TRAIN WHISTLE]

251
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:20,480
Huh? What?
I can't hear you!

252
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:24,780
Brother? Wait up!

253
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,560
See ya, Winry!

254
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,480
Okay...jeez.

255
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,300
Come back, Edward!

256
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:32,200
What were you saying?

257
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:39,880
The next time I make you cry,
I hope they'll be tears of joy!

258
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:42,320
Then Al and I will be
back in our normal bodies,

259
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:44,960
and I'll make you cry
out of sheer happiness!

260
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:46,260
That's a promise!

261
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:49,480
[LAUGHS]

262
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:03,120
Give me a new arm and a leg.

263
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:05,320
I need one year.

264
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:06,560
Well...

265
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:09,280
There's no turning
back for us now, brother.

266
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:14,600
What are you crying for, Winry?

267
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:36,980
All this time...have I been...

268
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:38,980
Falling for him?

269
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:48,080
Colonel!

270
00:17:48,180 --> 00:17:49,700
Get in the car.

271
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,820
Someone's badly injured.
I came to you because we need a doctor.

272
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:05,300
Got yourself in trouble again.
Just can't help yourself.

273
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:08,480
I know you have a family.
I wouldn't want to endanger them.

274
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:11,060
If you'd rather not get
involved, I'll understand.

275
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:14,800
Wait here. I'll get my instruments.

276
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:16,440
You sure about this?

277
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:22,300
My wife and I split up not long
after I came back from duty in Ishval.

278
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:27,700
You let her wander around
the sewers with her arm cut off?

279
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:30,020
Don't blame me if she gets lockjaw.

280
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:36,000
I'm afraid the only patients
I've had lately have been corpses,

281
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,100
so this might be a little rough.

282
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,900
[LAN FAN SCREAMING]

283
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:47,420
- I'm sorry—
- No, don't apologize.

284
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,860
I'm the one who suggested it, remember?

285
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:54,300
We both had something to
gain out of it, so it made sense.

286
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:56,900
When I went in search of immortality,

287
00:18:57,040 --> 00:19:00,240
I knew I must be ready
to make certain sacrifices.

288
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:04,840
But I...

289
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:07,220
I wasn't ready for this.

290
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:09,980
Lan Fan was, though.

291
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:12,820
She made the decision
that I was too weak to make.

292
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:18,220
[WHIMPERING]

293
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:21,180
[GASPS]
She's awake!

294
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,620
You okay? Is there anything we can do?

295
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:28,620
That old trap of yours worked pretty well.

296
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,620
But I'm useless without my arm.

297
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:36,300
I'm going to need to find a replacement.

298
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:42,880
You know, I can introduce
you to a great engineer.

299
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:52,020
I'm with the state military.

300
00:19:52,180 --> 00:19:53,840
Name's Colonel Roy Mustang.

301
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:59,300
And my name is Ling Yao,
the twelfth son of the Emperor of Xing.

302
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:01,940
I appreciate you finding a doctor.

303
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:03,460
It was no problem.

304
00:20:03,460 --> 00:20:05,840
Thank you for helping
us with the Ross incident.

305
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:09,860
And also...
for bringing this thing in.

306
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,660
Hey, what do we have here?

307
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:19,860
That's Gluttony. He's a Homunculus.

308
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:23,980
He and his friends
appear to have connections

309
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:26,380
among some of the
military's senior staff.

310
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:27,300
[GASP]

311
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:30,060
Just some, you say?
It goes far deeper than that.

312
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:32,860
Your Führer King Bradley?

313
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:35,560
I believe it's possible that
he's a Homunculus too.

314
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:36,880
[GASPS]

315
00:20:37,300 --> 00:20:38,780
I saw his eye.

316
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:41,680
The one under the patch,
it had an Ouroboros tattoo.

317
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:44,940
He and Gluttony came after us
and they were working together.

318
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:46,080
No way!

319
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:48,680
Our ruler? A Homunculus?

320
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:50,680
Although...

321
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:55,220
Bradley doesn't have the same sort of
inhuman presence that you get from Gluttony.

322
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:58,420
At his core, he still feels
like a regular person.

323
00:20:58,440 --> 00:21:03,080
Another thing, if the Führer is a
Homunculus, how can he possibly have a son?

324
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:07,300
It's said in that book that the Homunculi
have no reproductive capabilities.

325
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:11,220
No, the Führer's son Selim is adopted.

326
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:14,300
There's no direct blood relation
between him and his father.

327
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,480
[ROY SCOFFS]
AL: Huh?

328
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:20,600
Whether he's monster or human,

329
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:25,280
either way, these new developments will make
it easier to remove him from the seat of power.

330
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:28,480
First, we get information out of this one.

331
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:30,180
And I'll take his stone.

332
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:32,700
It may prove useful in treating my man.

333
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,320
Hey, you!

334
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:36,580
Lan Fan lost her arm to get him!

335
00:21:36,620 --> 00:21:39,340
He's our captive!
We're taking him back to Xing!

336
00:21:39,460 --> 00:21:41,840
Hold it!
He could help us get our bodies back!

337
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:44,020
We've been working on that for a long time.

338
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:46,300
I'm not gonna let you
just waltz off with him!

339
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:49,080
That's right!
Think about it, Ling.

340
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,460
You're an illegal alien!

341
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:52,060
I'm too old for this kind of thing.

342
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:54,620
Good luck, Mustang. I'm going home.

343
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:55,220
Listen to me...

344
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,620
Colonel Mustang.

345
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:59,960
Mustang was one who killed Lust.

346
00:22:00,060 --> 00:22:02,940
Mustang must pay for what he did to her!

347
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:13,300
Roy Mustang!

348
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:26,300
What was that?!

349
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:34,320
Let it all out, let it all out

350
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:38,760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

351
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

352
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:51,120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

353
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,680
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

354
00:22:56,680 --> 00:23:02,200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

355
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:11,960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

356
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:17,580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

357
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:23,480
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

358
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:31,540
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

359
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:33,820
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

360
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:39,340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

361
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:45,560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

362
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:53,200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

363
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:57,740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

364
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:02,920
What lies safely hidden behind lying eyes?

365
00:24:03,220 --> 00:24:06,280
Behind fake smiles,
and feigned friendship?

366
00:24:06,620 --> 00:24:09,220
Finding out will be no easy task.

367
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:13,840
Enter the forest, grope in
the darkness for the unknown.

368
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:17,380
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

369
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:21,120
Episode 24: Inside the Belly

370
00:24:21,580 --> 00:24:23,300
If you move carelessly...

371
00:24:23,320 --> 00:24:28,180
Nothing but pain will await
you in the inky blackness.
